---
import Reveal from './react/Reveal.tsx'
---

<section id="about" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 sm:py-24">
  <Reveal client:load>
    <div class="mb-12">
      <span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">// about</span>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-100 sm:text-3xl">Who I am</h2>
    </div>
  </Reveal>

  <Reveal client:load delay={0.1}>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-base text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed sm:text-lg">
      <p>
        I'm Craig Albertson, a <span class="text-zinc-200">QA Analyst</span> with 4 years of experience
        in functional testing, regression testing, and ensuring software reliability across
        complex systems. I've spent my career breaking things on purpose so users never
        have to experience them breaking by accident. Most recently at <span class="text-zinc-200">Proctor Loan Protector</span>
        and previously at <span class="text-zinc-200">Infosys Limited</span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Currently pursuing a <span class="text-zinc-200">Master of Science in Artificial Intelligence</span>
        through Udacity's Institute of AI &amp; Technology, I'm expanding into the world of ML and AI
        engineering. My goal is to work at the intersection of quality assurance and intelligent
        systems — building AI that's not just powerful, but
        <span class="text-zinc-200">tested, reliable, and trustworthy</span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        As part of my reskilling journey, I relearned <span class="text-zinc-200">Python</span> from the
        ground up and have been building hands-on AI projects through Udacity — including
        implementing a <span class="text-zinc-200">Transformer model from scratch using PyTorch</span>.
        These projects have given me practical experience with neural network architecture,
        model training, and the same rigorous evaluation mindset I bring to QA.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Reveal>
</section>